# rhwp change tracking for why-hwp: read it from HWPX and write it to HWP.
# Base: rhwp 981ce66b4 (v0.9.1) after the source edits in wasm/patch-rhwp.sh and
# wasm/patches/rhwp-layout.patch to rhwp-trackchange2.patch; apply this after
# rhwp-trackchange2.patch.
# Zero-context diff (apply with git apply --unidiff-zero). Hunks touch no file
# of rhwp-trackchange2.patch and change no line that rhwp-trackchange.patch added.
#
# - hh:trackChanges and hh:trackChangeAuthors are read into
#   DocInfo::track_changes and DocInfo::track_change_authors at their ids.
# - hp:insertBegin/End and hp:deleteBegin/End become range tags of kind 0x10
#   and 0x11 (TcId in the low 24 bits), hp:run/@charTcId and hp:p/@paraTcId
#   become kind 0x12 and 0x13, and hp:p/@merged="1" goes to PARA_HEADER
#   offset 22. Order, ends and empty ranges follow the HWP Hancom Office wrote
#   from the same HWPX (rhwp sample issue5169, 590 paragraphs, and t2).
# - An HWP save writes TRACK_CHANGE_AUTHOR and TRACK_CHANGE records from the
#   model when the DocInfo holds no raw ones (an HWP source keeps its own), and
#   ID_MAPPINGS counts them.
# - rhwp projects hidden tracked changes out of the IR it shows. An HWP or HWPX
#   export of an HWPX document that is still as loaded reads the file again
#   without that projection, so deleted text stays inside its range tags.
